and checksums with the archived manifests when preparing complete Corresponding Source.

Reproduce with the accompanying build script after copying this resource folder:
python3 build_torrent_worker.py --rebuild --output-directory ./rebuilt
The script extracts the dependency ZIP as khua-torrent beside server, applies its
patch, and changes only the existing torrent replacement to ../khua-torrent in
the temporary build's go.mod. All other module versions and go.sum stay fixed.
Build from that patched server directory using Go go1.26.4:
GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.4 GOWORK=off GOFLAGS= GOEXPERIMENT= GOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64 GOARM64=v8.0 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -mod=readonly -trimpath -buildvcs=false -tags=nosqlite -ldflags="-s -w -checklinkname=0 -buildid= -X server/version.Version=MatriX.147-khua.4" -o TorrServer ./cmd
The Khua source also includes Scripts/build_torrent_worker.py and
Scripts/prepare_torrent_worker.sh to verify, patch and build these pinned inputs.
The build does not regenerate web assets, update API docs, or run go mod tidy.

