Nonce-tagged bounded prefetch responses report a capacity stop through the next
authenticated playback-window ACK. Proof includes the exact file, finite range,
request UUID and successfully delivered byte frontier. Only a real quota EOF
before the requested end is eligible; client cancellation, writer failure,
ordinary file EOF, missing windows and untagged requests produce no proof.
One event is retained per consumer, replaced by a new request and cleared on
release or file changes; refreshing a window preserves it until consumed.

Finite managed prefetch readers bind the validated range start before cache
registration and remain inactive during HTTP metadata seeks. The first actual
read starts bounded lookahead, so a temporary byte-zero cursor does not consume
cache quota. The watchdog checks parked state and resumes readers under the same
reader lock, preventing a completed bounded fill from being reactivated at its
upper boundary and evicting retained bytes. Core and whole-file save reader
construction and seek behavior remain unchanged.
